        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c2_its_central_contribution_concept_con",
          "text": "Its central contribution is the concept of context shift, which describes the semantically meaningful upstream factors, sample selection bias, adversarial perturbation, and non-stationarity, that drive the distribution shifts we observe.",
